      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Join me, if your friend is set to it but it is not their private world then it will not send a invite to you, if your world is a Invite Only, then only the one who made it can accept your invites, if its set to Invite+ then anyone in that world can receive an invite, if they are in a friends only world and you are not friends with the owner then it will not send an invite, also if your status is red it will decline the invites, and the invites take a moment, 10-60secs, their is also a little thing if they player cap is full then it might not send you an invite to the world, make sure your social list is expanded and it reloaded itself, there could also be an \"out of date\" status or \"incorrectly label\" status that the servers and your client have not sync up to each other, thats why you should go to Friends+ or invite+ and make sure your status is set to green or blue, I normally request an invite and then i wait about 10-30 secs then i open and close my mini menu a bit and it works, but it will not work if its invite only and you request someone whos not the owner, and if your friend is in a \"private\" world but its really a friends only then they will not be able to send a request, so in recap Join me works if they are the owner or if its invite+ and you dont have your status on red, theres a 2-5% it wont work regardless but thats more of the servers and your client not sync",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
